The '''2026 Hillingdon London Borough Council election''' took place on 7 May 2026.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Thomas |first=Dee |title=Hillingdon Council elections 2026 |url=https://pre.hillingdon.gov.uk/elections-voting/hillingdon-council-elections-2026 |access-date=2026-01-19 |website=Hillingdon Council |language=en}}</ref> All 53 members of [[Hillingdon London Borough Council]] were up for election. The elections took place alongside [[2026 London local elections|local elections in the other London boroughs]] and [[2026 United Kingdom local elections|elections to local authorities across the United Kingdom]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Number of councils that have requested delay to local elections revealed - is yours one of them? |url=https://news.sky.com/story/local-elections-2026-over-a-third-of-councils-offered-a-delay-have-requested-one-is-yours-on-the-list-13494762 |access-date=2026-01-19 |website=Sky News |language=en}}</ref>

== Background ==
In the [[2022 Hillingdon London Borough Council election|previous election in 2022]], the [[Conservative Party (UK)|Conservative Party]] maintained its control of the council despite losing 4 seats to the [[Labour Party (UK)|Labour Party]].<ref>{{Cite news |title=Hillingdon result - Local Elections 2022 |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/election/2022/england/councils/E09000017 |access-date=2026-01-19 |work=BBC News |language=en-GB}}</ref>

